p: 15px;">
In the past, personalization and history on Play were managed by Web &amp; =
App Activity (WAA) settings in your Google Account. Going forward, WAA will=
 no longer control Play personalization and Play History. Instead, you=E2=
=80=99ll be able to manage those settings directly on Play, and you=E2=80=
=99ll see this change in your account in the next few days. <a target=3D_bl=
ank style=3D"color: #1a73e8;" href=3Dhttp://support.google.com/googleplay?p=
=3Dpersonalize_play_migration>Learn more about Play personalization and Pla=
y History</a>
</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td align=3Dleft valign=3Dtop style=3D"font-size: 14px; line-height: 24px; =
font-family: Roboto, Helvetica, Arial, sans-serif; color:#414347;padding-to=
p: 15px;">
When the transition happens for your account, your Play settings will be ba=
sed on the most recent choice you made in WAA, so your experience will stay=
 the same. If you have WAA turned on during the transition, which is happen=
ing over the next few days, then your Play personalization and Play History=
 settings will be on, and if WAA is off, then Play personalization and Play=
 History will be off. As before, you=E2=80=99ll be able to choose how long =
your activity is saved in your Play History and if you want to delete it fr=
om Play History manually or automatically.
</td>
</tr>
